{
  "id": "pokemon-center-10th-anniversary",
  "name": "Pokémon Center 10th Anniversary",
  "category": "retailer_promotion",
  "description": {
    "text": "To mark ten years since the Pokémon Centers opened, the Pokémon Center stores in Japan gave a card to each shopper four times, one per person while stocks lasted, all four made by Yuka Morii. From 30 May to 15 June 2008 each of the five stores, Tokyo, Yokohama, Osaka, Nagoya and Fukuoka, gave its own slightly different Pikachu, 098 to 102/DP-P. Charmander 124/DP-P followed from 22 August 2008, Squirtle 009/DPt-P, picked by a vote over Meowth, from 14 November 2008, and Bulbasaur 030/DPt-P from 4 April 2009, when shoppers who brought any two different cards of the four got a Pokémon Card Game coin.\n\nEach card's attack brings a card from the deck: Pikachu's Shopping (おかいもの) finds a Pokémon Tool, Charmander's Little Errand (ちいさなおつかい) a basic Energy, Squirtle's Souvenir Pick (おみやげえらび) keeps one of the top two cards, and Bulbasaur's Present (プレゼント) takes any card on a coin flip.",
